# Raw-byte SHA pins: the frozen-contract configs, immutable results, pinned docs and
# pinned sources carry SHA-256 digests computed over the repository's LF byte layout.
# On a `core.autocrlf=true` host (this Windows checkout) Git rewrites text files to
# CRLF in the working tree, which breaks every one of those pins even though the
# content is identical. `-text` disables end-of-line conversion for these paths so the
# working-tree bytes are the pinned bytes on every machine. See
# docs/prospective-live-data-plumbing-2026-11-21.md (test environment section).
config/** -text
results/** -text
docs/** -text
snapshots/** -text
# Every Python source is byte-pinned somewhere (frozen evaluation contracts, result
# provenance maps, frozen parser hashes), and every one of those pins was computed
# over LF bytes; a CRLF working tree breaks them. LF sources need no conversion on
# any host.
src/** -text
tests/** -text
# Pins computed over the CRLF bytes of the original Windows checkout (module-constant
# pins in src/fpl/validate/dev_v2_real_sot.py, and the frozen Phase 4 source pins that
# frozen_source_checks.py documents as the exact original Windows checkout): these
# check out as CRLF deterministically. Later lines override the src/** rule above.
results/v2_team_environment_development.json text eol=crlf
src/fpl/validate/points_harness.py text eol=crlf
src/fpl/models/sdp_environment.py text eol=crlf
src/fpl/models/price_starter_prior.py text eol=crlf
src/fpl/models/minutes_shrinkage.py text eol=crlf
src/fpl/models/minutes_v3.py text eol=crlf
